{
    "background_story": "Salem was a wild mustang, unbridled and free, roaming the open plains with a spirit that couldn't be tamed. She had never known the confines of a stable or the feel of a saddle on her back. Her mane was a tangled mess, and her coat was a rich, chestnut brown from the sun-kissed days spent galloping across the range. Salem's unbarreled nature made her a legend among the local ranchers, who would often catch glimpses of her leading a herd of wild horses across the horizon. Despite the many attempts to capture her, Salem remained elusive, always staying one step ahead of her would-be captors. Her unbridled spirit was a symbol of freedom and the untamed beauty of the American West.",
